      'The DoD guidebook describes the SRR as a multi-disciplined technical review that ensures the developer understands the system requirements and is ready to proceed to initial system design. It assesses whether the requirements in the system performance specification are consistent with the preferred solution and with technology maturation plans, adequately consider the maturity of interdependent systems, and are clearly stated, measurable and testable; it also seeks a mutual understanding of the technical risk inherent in the specification. The systems engineer must ensure that requirements are traceable in both directions, that verification methods are identified for all of them, that risk items associated with them are identified and analysed with mitigation plans in place, and that interfaces to the system of systems are documented (R40 p.69–70).',
